================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers only the material written by the copyright holder
for this project: everything under `src/`, `tests/`, the generated ports under
`ports/`, the result artifacts under `results/` and `certificates/`, and all
Markdown documentation at the repository root.

It does NOT relicense two categories of material that this repository merely
carries or depends on. Both are declared in full in PRIOR-WORK.md.

1. Vendored input data — `corpus/*.xlsx`

   17 municipal finance workbooks published by the Commonwealth of
   Massachusetts, Division of Local Services, at
   mass.gov/info-details/municipal-finance-tools-templates-calculators

   These are public records of a US state government, reproduced here
   unmodified so that the evaluation can be rerun without network access.
   They are not the copyright holder's work and are not licensed under the
   terms above. No claim of authorship or ownership is made over them.

2. Third-party dependencies — not vendored, installed from PyPI via `uv.lock`

   Each is used unmodified, as an ordinary library import, under its own
   licence:

     openpyxl        MIT
     formulas        EUPL-1.1+
     hypothesis      MPL-2.0
     numpy           BSD-3-Clause
     scipy           BSD-3-Clause
     schedula        EUPL-1.1+
     numpy-financial BSD-3-Clause

   `formulas` and `schedula` are EUPL-licensed. This project links to them as
   unmodified libraries and distributes no copy or derivative of either, so no
   EUPL source-distribution obligation is triggered here. Anyone who modifies
   and redistributes those libraries takes on their obligations, not these.
